---
title: "OpenAPI Compose deployment lifecycle"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Serving
    lg1: Upgrade
    lg2: Provisioning
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 purple
  class lg2 blue
  s0: Provisioning shared network
  s1: Provisioning Obot dependencies
  s2: Provisioning service authentication
  s3: Provisioning Obot
  s4: Provisioning Workers
  s5: Both stacks ready, traffic closed
  s6: OpenAPI traffic admitted
  s7: Rolling upgrade, capacity retained
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: operator creates the explicit shared network
  s1 --> s0: the shared network disappears
  s1 --> s2: PostgreSQL passes readiness
  s2 --> s3: the service CA becomes trusted
  s3 --> s2: service authentication is withdrawn
  s3 --> s4: the Obot replica passes readiness
  s4 --> s5: the Worker passes readiness
  s5 --> s6: an OpenAPI request is admitted after every gate holds
  s5 --> s7: a one-at-a-time Obot upgrade starts or a one-at-a-time Worker upgrade starts
  s6 --> s5: the OpenAPI request completes
  s7 --> s5: the upgraded replica is healthy again
  s7 --> s6: an OpenAPI request is admitted after every gate holds
  s6 --> s7: the OpenAPI request completes
  class s0 blue
  class s1 blue
  class s2 blue
  class s3 blue
  class s4 blue
  class s5 blue
  class s6 teal
  class s7 purple
